L000310	the large $N$ limit is stable for $g^2 \leq \frac{1}{15 \pi}$. Near the critical coupling, it corresponds to 2D string theory with $1/\alpha'$ equal to the curvature of the potential at the local maximum; hence, $\alpha'=1$.
L000311	The absence of $\mathbb{Z}_2$ symmetry makes us expect a single Regge trajectory.
L000312	
L000313	To  study the MO equation for \eqref{cubicpot} at the critical coupling $g_c=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{15 \pi}}$, it is again convenient to change to the time-of-flight variable \eqref{eq:time-of-flight}: $x=\frac{1}{6g_c}\left (1-3\tanh^2\frac{\tau}{2}\right)$, and
L000314	now $\tau$ runs from $0$ to $\infty$. The critical MO Hamiltonian is
L000315	\begin{equation}\label{decoupledH-phi3}
L000316	    \mathcal{H}_{\rm cubic}(p,\tau)=
L000317	    p\coth(\pi p\tanh{\frac{\tau}{2}})+
L000318	    \frac{\tau}{\pi}\coth\tau - \frac{2\tau}{\sinh\tau}-\frac{3}{\pi}\ .
L000319	\end{equation}
