L000349	To see the two Regge trajectories analytically (i.e., to see the alternating terms in the expression for energy levels \eqref{eq:regge-phi4}, \eqref{eq:regge-dw}), it is necessary to use more sophisticated analytical methods, one of which is the integrability-based Fateev-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov (FLZ) method developed for the 't Hooft model \cite{Fateev:2009jf,Litvinov:2024riz,Artemev:2025cev}. Note that our analytical formulas reproduce the spectrum of short strings with very high accuracy (see table \ref{tab:numerics}). We expect corrections to our formulas to be exponentially small in contrast
L000350	to the larger corrections to the WKB eigenvalues of the 't Hooft equation \cite{Fateev:2009jf,Litvinov:2024riz,Artemev:2025cev}.
